Grove PATCH-36: a coin that is not active this session defers a bid, never kills it

Grove runs host-wallet coins (ZEPH, ZANO) only while the app's own wallet
process is up. The vault is locked when the swap node autostarts, so those coins
PARK for that start, and the supervisor restarts the node once the wallet comes
up. Upstream has never had a coin disappear under an in-flight swap, and treats
it as a broken bid in two places.

WHAT IT COST (2026-09-13, mainnet, the ZANO<>LTC swap)

This node was waiting to publish the ZANO lock (tx B), retrying every ~3 min
(the PATCH-35 identity refusal). The app was closed at ~15:51. At the 16:27
restart ZANO was parked, and loading the bid failed:

    Failed to activate bid! Error: 16
    basicswap.util.InactiveCoin: 16

loadFromDB's handler then ran deactivateBid, whose

    DELETE FROM actions WHERE linked_id = :bid_id

(UPDATE ... active_ind = 2 under debug) retired the bid's queued
SEND_XMR_SWAP_LOCK_TX_B retry. The unpark restart four minutes later loaded the
bid as in progress again, but nothing re-queues that action, so the node never
tried the ZANO lock again. It sat until the offerer refunded 15 hours later.
The failure repeated at three later starts. So even with PATCH-35 in place, this
restart alone would have failed the swap.

The second place is checkQueuedActions. An action that comes due while its coin
is parked raises InactiveCoin, falls into the generic except, sets the bid to
BID_ERROR and is deleted with the processed rows.

THE FIX

- loadFromDB: InactiveCoin during activation logs "activation deferred" and
  leaves the bid untouched: no BID_ERROR, no deactivateBid, so its queued actions
  survive. The next start with the coin active activates it exactly as before.
- checkQueuedActions: InactiveCoin keeps the action, in the same retry list
  TemporaryError uses, and does not error the bid. The action runs once the coin
  is back.

Every other activation failure and action failure is handled exactly as before.

Scope: InactiveCoin only. It is raised by BasicSwap.ci() for a coin with no
interface this session, and never by a swap step's own failure.

Verified by verify-redeem-recovery-patches.py (PWNDA-PATCH-36 section), which
drives the real loadFromDB and checkQueuedActions against stubbed DB cursors.
Each case has a negative control: a ValueError must still error the bid.

Upstream candidate: possibly. Upstream can hit it too, whenever a coin is removed
from basicswap.json while one of its bids is in progress.

diff --git a/basicswap/basicswap.py b/basicswap/basicswap.py
--- a/basicswap/basicswap.py
+++ b/basicswap/basicswap.py
@@ -3927,4 +3927,26 @@
                     try:
                         self.activateBid(cursor, bid)
+                    except InactiveCoin as ex:
+                        # PWNDA-PATCH-36: a coin that is not active THIS session
+                        # (a Grove host-wallet coin parks while the vault is
+                        # locked) defers the bid; it is not a broken bid. The
+                        # handler below sets BID_ERROR and runs deactivateBid,
+                        # which DELETEs the bid's queued actions -- on
+                        # 2026-09-13 that retired a ZANO lock retry nothing ever
+                        # re-queued, and the swap waited for a refund. Leave the
+                        # bid and its actions for the next start.
+                        self.swaps_in_progress.pop(bid.bid_id, None)
+                        coin_name = Coins(ex.coinid).name
+                        self.log.warning(
+                            f"Deferring bid {self.log.id(bid.bid_id)}: {coin_name} is not "
+                            "active this session (PWNDA-PATCH-36)"
+                        )
+                        self.logEvent(
+                            Concepts.BID,
+                            bid.bid_id,
+                            EventLogTypes.ERROR,
+                            f"Activation deferred: {coin_name} is not active this session",
+                            cursor,
+                        )
                     except Exception as ex:
                         self.logException(f"Failed to activate bid! Error: {ex}")
@@ -11491,7 +11512,18 @@
                 except TemporaryError as ex:
                     self.log.warning(
                         f"checkQueuedActions temporary error for {self.log.id(linked_id)}: {ex}"
                     )
                     retry_action_ids.append(action_id)
+                except InactiveCoin as ex:
+                    # PWNDA-PATCH-36: the action's coin is parked this session.
+                    # Falling through to the generic handler below would set the
+                    # bid to BID_ERROR and delete the action. Keep it for when
+                    # the coin is back, like a TemporaryError.
+                    self.log.debug(
+                        f"checkQueuedActions: {Coins(ex.coinid).name} is not active this "
+                        f"session; keeping action {action_type} for "
+                        f"{self.log.id(linked_id)} (PWNDA-PATCH-36)"
+                    )
+                    retry_action_ids.append(action_id)
                 except Exception as ex:
                     err_msg = f"checkQueuedActions failed: {ex}"
